   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to forwarding reports of abuse to the social services district charged with the care, custody, or guardianship of the child",
    "basePrintNo": "S4172",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4172-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §424, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4172\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the social services law, in relation\nto forwarding reports of abuse to the social services district charged\nwith the care, custody, or guardianship of the child\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide to the authorized agency and any other social services\ndistrict charged with the care, custody or guardianship of a child the\nreport of suspected child abuse or, maltreatment of such child in the\ncare, custody or guardianship of an authorized agency where the\nauthorized agency is not the social services district in which the\nhome is located.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one amends subdivision 6 of section 424 of the social services\nlaw, as amended by chapter 602 of the laws of 2008, to add a new\nsubdivision to require child protective services to ascertain whether\na child named in a report of suspected child abuse or maltreatment or\nany other child in the same home is in the care, custody or\nguardianship of an authorized agency. Where such authorized agency is\nnot the social services district in which the home is located, the\nreport shall be forwarded as soon as possible to such authorized\nagency and any other social services district charged with the care,\ncustody or guardianship of the child or other children in the home.\nIn addition, such authorized agency and local social services district\nmust be notified as to whether such report is indicated or unfounded\nin accordance with subdivision seven of section 424.  Nothing in the\nsubdivision, however, shall require such social services district to\ninvestigate or participate in the investigation of such report.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe care and custody of a child may be transferred to an authorized\nagency, i.e. placed in foster care. There is no requirement that the\nauthorized agency charged with the care and custody of the child must\nbe located in the same social services district in which the child's\nhome is located.\n\nA problem arises when the foster home is the subject of a report of\nchild abuse or maltreatment and the foster home is not located in the\nsocial services district that placed the child in the foster home.\nThere is no mechanism under current law that requires notification of\nsuch report to be provided to the placing social services district.\nAbsent information that the foster home may be the subject of a report\nof child abuse or maltreatment, the placing social services district\nmay continue to place children in the care and custody of that foster\nhome.\n\nBy requiring that the authorized agency and any social services\ndistrict charged with the care, custody or guardianship of a child\nreceive a copy of a report of suspected abuse or maltreatment of the\nchild where the authorized agency is not the social services district\nin which the home is located, we can close gaps in communication\nbetween and among authorized agencies and social services districts\nresponsible for the safety and welfare of our children. Placing\nagencies must be informed of reports of suspected abuse or\nmaltreatment involving homes in which they have placed children so\nthat they do not unwittingly place additional children in a situation\nthat risks subjecting them to abuse or maltreatment.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
